# NOTE: this copy is NOT the one that ships.  fuzix-basefs.pkg installs
# /etc/rc from Standalone/filesystem-src/etc-files/rc, and the two have
# drifted; edit that one for anything that must reach a card.
umask 022
fsck -a -y /
setdate
remount -n / rw
prtroot >/etc/mtab
# No swapon. Swap is not a device any more: the kernel allocates a
# region the size of the process out of the PSRAM heap and memcpy's
# into it. Nothing here has to know a size, which is just as well - the
# 14208 that used to be on this line had to agree with a split computed
# in three other files, and a stale value would have had swap writing
# through whatever came next.
# USB keyboard layout: us uk de fr es be
picoctl keymap uk
# Num lock is a property of the KEYBOARD: one with no numeric keypad (a
# Raspberry Pi keyboard, most laptop-style boards) overlays one onto
# 7890/uiop/jkl;/m while num lock is on.  The kernel turns it off by
# itself for a keyboard that declares no num lock LED, but plenty of
# keypad-less keyboards declare one anyway - so "picoctl numlock off"
# records the answer per keyboard in /etc/numlock and this replays it.
# The kernel does not write files; that file is the whole of the memory.
picoctl numlock --load
# NOTE: keyboard auto-repeat (kbdrate) does NOT belong here - rc runs
# before init has given it a controlling terminal, and kbdrate opens
# /dev/tty, so it fails with "failed ioctl".  It lives in /etc/profile
# instead.  The compiled-in default (600ms then 100ms) already matches,
# so this is only for retuning.
#Uncomment if you have multiple file systems
#fsck -a
#mount -a
>/var/run/utmp
